infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Binding a global enhancer: new vs APP_GUARD
  desc Same global scope, not equivalent — one lives outside DI and injects nothing, the other is built by the container
  compares
    - label new RolesGuard() in main.ts
      children
        - label Outside the DI container
          desc You construct the instance yourself, Nest never sees it
        - label Injects nothing
          desc Reflector and UsersService are whatever you passed — usually null
        - label Defaults open
          desc Null service, role check throws, every user becomes admin
        - label Safe only without deps
          desc Acceptable for a dependency-free enhancer only
    - label provide APP_GUARD useClass
      children
        - label Inside the DI container
          desc Nest instantiates it as a real provider
        - label Deps inject normally
          desc Reflector and UsersService resolve from the container
        - label Global and DI-aware
          desc Applies to every route with full injection
        - label One token per kind
          desc APP_GUARD, APP_INTERCEPTOR, APP_PIPE, APP_FILTER
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
